  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth Empowerment on SRHR (YES!) Advancing the Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights of Young People in Sindh and Punjab</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of this project is to improve sexual and reproductive health outcomes of young people in Pakistan by increasing access to information and services, and decreasing associated stigma. The program will target young people, particularly girls, 12 years and above through school based interventions, young people between 16 and 24 years at the community level, young people 16 and above through digital and other communications platforms, medical and nursing students who are most commonly 18-22 years, and policy makers/decision makers who are relevant to enacting policy change and developing public programs that impact the SRHR of young people.</narrative>
  </description>
